Maran: Sira!
Sira: Oh, hey Maran. What's up?
Maran: I made some manuk pansuh for you!
Maran: They're a bit cold now because I had to wait for the ceremony to be over, but it's still good!
Sira: Maran... What did I do to deserve a friend like you?
Maran: It's the least that I can do.
Maran: Here's one more for Jitendra. You guys have been working hard lately!
Sira: Thanks, Maran. I'll give it to Jitendra.
[signal arg="manuk_pansuh"]
(A lukewarm manuk pansuh acquired)
Sira: There's been a lot of work because my dad is planning to open a new farming location.
Sira: And, well, because of me too.
Maran: Oh, I'm sure he just wants to make sure everyone is okay.
Maran: I wouldn't even dare to step a foot in the Sacred Forest, Sira...
Maran: How are you able to do it alone?
Sira: I'm not always alone.
Sira: I still have Jitendra to annoy whenever I need to let some steam off.
Maran: That poor guy. He's injured and you're still bothering him?
Sira: He's the one who's always mean to me though...
Maran: Ehehehe, I'm just kidding, Sira.  I know you both are always butting heads with each other.
Maran: How is he doing? I heard he fell off a tree again after breaking his leg.
Sira: Still stubborn that he can handle it like the man he is.
Sira: I think everyone heard him groaning in pain at night.
Maran: It's hard to unhear it when everyone sleeps under the same roof *sighs*.
Sira: I should get going then. Thank you for the manuk pansuh, Maran.
Maran: Anytime!